+        // WPA3-Personal (and any mode carrying an SAE component) is validated by pWHM's
+        // object-level "on action validate" hook (wld_ap_validateSecurity_ovf ->
+        // wld_ap_sec_checkSecConfigParams), which cross-checks ModeEnabled against
+        // KeyPassPhrase/SAEPassphrase using the object's *current* param values.
+        //
+        // Within a single update_object() htable transaction, amxd applies/validates the
+        // individual param writes in htable (hash-based) order, NOT the insertion order of
+        // add_child() calls above. If ModeEnabled happens to be applied/validated before
+        // SAEPassphrase/KeyPassPhrase land on the object, the cross-field validator sees the
+        // OLD (often empty, for a freshly-created VAP) passphrase value and rejects the whole
